        "original_id": "806cdb48-96f4-590d-b3be-8e051eb706c9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Guiping, Hailin, Guangxi, Heilongjiang, Mudanjiang, China\n- Rivers: Qian River, Yu Jiang, Xun, Xi Jiang, Hongshui River\n- Languages: Eastern Hongshuihe Zhuang, Northern Tai\n\nFacts:\n- Guiping is a county-level city in eastern Guangxi, China.\n- Hailin is a county-level city in Heilongjiang province in northeast China, and it is part of Mudanjiang prefecture-level city.\n- At Guiping, the Qian River is joined by the more southerly Yu Jiang to form the Xun branch of the Xi Jiang.\n- Eastern Hongshuihe Zhuang is a Northern Tai language spoken in Guangxi, China, south of the Qian River and the eastern stretch of the Hongshui River.",
